is int(s, base) (CPython's PyLong_FromString: whitespace, a sign, underscores between"] [369 1 "// digits, the 0x/0o/0b prefixes with base 0 or their own base)."] [374 1 "// ParseIntBytes is int(b, base) of a bytes-like object: its bytes as ASCII text, the error naming them as bytes"] [375 1 "// (_PyLong_FromBytes' %R of a bytes object; queue 286: test_int's test_error_message)."] [380 1 "// ParseIntStr is int(s, base) of a str: _PyUnicode_TransformDecimalAndSpaceToASCII first (queue 286: a Unicode"] [381 1 "// decimal digit as its ASCII digit, a Unicode space as ' ', any other non-ASCII character invalid; test_decimal's"] [382 1 "// test_unicode_digits), the error naming the str as given. An ASCII str (its flag) is parsed as it is: no pass over"] [383 1 "// its text before the digits limit's check (under goi an interpreted pass; test_int's"] [384 1 "// test_denial_of_service_prevented_str_to_int times the refusal of 1.2M digits against a conversion)."] [406 1 "// parseInt is ParseInt of text, its error naming orig's value."] [440 2 "// long_from_string_base: the digits limit for every base not a power of two (py-core-1124: test_int's"] [441 2 "// test_int_from_other_bases)"] [524 1 "// intNew is int(), int(x), int(s, base)."] [535 3 "// long_new_impl: PyNumber_AsSsize_t(obase, NULL), __index__ (a float a TypeError), clipped beyond (py-core-1124:"] [536 3 "// test_int's test_int_base_bad_types, test_int_base_indexable)"] [551 3 "// long_new_impl: a str (a subclass too), bytes or bytearray (theirs too), any other object a TypeError (queue"] [552 3 "// 286: a str subclass was refused, a memoryview taken; test_int's test_non_numeric_input_types)"] [576 1 "// newIntSubclass makes an instance of an int subclass; PY5c sets it (classes' instances)."] [603 1 "// ToInt is int(x): an int's value, __int__, __index__, a float truncated, a str or bytes parsed."] [606 3 "// PyNumber_Long: an exact int as it is; a subclass's nb_int, its own __int__ (int's gives the value; queue 537:"] [607 3 "// one that returns a strict subclass of int is deprecated, test_int's test_int_returns_int_subclass)"] [632 2 "// a str subclass, a bytearray, any other buffer (PyNumber_Long's PyUnicode_Check and the buffer's"] [633 2 "// _PyLong_FromBytes; queue 286: int() of a str subclass was a TypeError)"] [643 1 "// floatToInt is int(f): truncated toward zero."] [659 1 "// Index is operator.index(o): an int, or __index__'s."] [677 1 "// IndexInt is Index's value as an int (an OverflowError beyond, CPython's \"cannot fit 'int' into an"] [678 1 "// index-sized integer\")."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[90 25] [158 17] [162 17] [169 17] [307 22] [315 25] [481 20] [481 36] [553 30] [554 41] [557 31] [559 41] [566 28] [605 22] [608 19] [626 24] [634 22] [637 24] [661 22] [664 30] [669 23]]} (go/file "int.go" :imports [


